on unless I can win outright.\n\n\n", 'output': 'Evaluation: My teammate (Previous Player) has only 3 cards left and just played an Ace. This is a strong move likely intended to either win the trick or force a top card from the Landlord. As the player acting immediately after my teammate and before the Landlord, I should not interfere with my teammate\'s potential win. Beating the Ace with my 2 or Red Joker would be counterproductive: it would waste my control cards and remove my teammate\'s control of the game. By passing, I force the Landlord (Next Player) to either spend a high card (2 or Black Joker) or allow my teammate to win the trick and potentially finish the game. If the Landlord does play a high card, I am in a good position to beat them with my Red Joker afterwards.\n\nReason: Do not beat your teammate\'s high card (Ace) when they are close to winning (3 cards left). Let the Landlord deal with it.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": []}'}
